\fIqnews\fR reads GLEP\ 42 news items for the configured repositories.
It is a small C equivalent of \fBeselect news\fR that needs neither
\fBeselect\fR nor Python.
.P
It understands three actions; with no action, \fBlist\fR is assumed:
.TP
.B list
List the available news items, marking which are unread.
.TP
.B count
Print the number of unread news items.
.TP
.B read \fR[\fBall\fR|\fI<item>\fR ...]
Display news item(s) and mark them read. With no argument every
currently unread item is shown; \fBall\fR shows every item, read or not;
or name one or more \fI<item>\fR identifiers to show just those.
.P
Read and unread state is tracked per repository under
\fI${ROOT}/var/lib/gentoo/news\fR, the same location Portage and
\fBeselect news\fR use, so the two stay consistent.